// regnamed_decl.cla: toolbox-integration Task 1 (Feature A) accept
// fixture -- a named `reg(...)` clause parses and checks clean. Not swept
// by driver_test.go's TestClarusModules glob (`*_test.cla` only, this
// file deliberately isn't named that way), so it's exercised ad hoc via
// scripts/clarus-run.sh / a crossgen-style current-source build (see the
// Task 1 report) rather than any automated Go test -- Step 3 of the brief
// uses it as the RED check (today's compiler fails to parse `reg(`) and
// Step 5 as the GREEN check (current-source clarusc parses, checks, and
// runs it). Declaration-only: TbGestalt is never called here (calls land
// in Task 2's own goldens, once cg68k grows named-clause codegen), so
// this only exercises parse.cla/ast.cla/ir.cla/check.cla, not cg68k.cla.
// The declaration's SHAPE is illustrative only -- pack3-standardfile Task
// 5a proved the real Gestalt trap returns its response in A0, not through
// an A1 pointer, so do not copy this as a Gestalt transcription; see
// toolbox/osutils.cla for the real declaration pair.
external func TbGestalt(selector: int, response: ptr): word =
    trap 0xA1AD reg(d0: selector, a1: response) ret d0

on App.startCLI(args: list of string) {
    alert("ok")
}
